            <ArticleTitle>Intravascular ultrasound-guided retrograde wiring for chronic total occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>214-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.22227</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a retrograde wiring technique, using intravascular ultrasound, for a blunt chronic total occlusion with a side branch at the site of occlusion of which the operator has difficulty of awareness of the proper re-entry point with the retrograde wire angiographically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
